# Rust Rules

## Banned Patterns

| Pattern | Do Instead |
|---------|------------|
| `.unwrap()` in production code | `?` operator or explicit `match`. `.unwrap()` allowed only in `#[cfg(test)]`. |
| `.expect()` in production code | `?` with `.context()` (`anyhow`) or typed error (`thiserror`). |
| `.clone()` to satisfy borrow checker | Fix lifetimes, use `Arc`, or restructure ownership. |
| `println!` / `eprintln!` | `tracing::info!`, `tracing::debug!`, `tracing::warn!`, `tracing::error!`. |
| Blocking I/O in `async fn` | Wrap in `tokio::task::spawn_blocking`. No `std::fs` in async context. |
| Raw `String` / `PathBuf` across layers | Use typed domain values. Parse into domain types at boundaries. |
| Direct S3/HTTP for object store | Use `opendal::Operator` via `src/storage/`. No raw `reqwest`/`aws-sdk-s3`. |

## Error Boundaries

```text
src/main.rs, src/cli/   → anyhow::Result  (CLI orchestration)
src/domain/, src/scan/,
src/lakehouse/, ...      → thiserror       (typed domain errors)
```

NEVER mix: do not return `anyhow::Error` from library modules.
Do not use `thiserror` in `main.rs`.

## Async Safety

- No `std::fs::read`, `std::fs::write`, or other blocking calls inside `async fn`.
- Use `tokio::fs` or wrap in `tokio::task::spawn_blocking`.
- CPU-heavy work (hashing, compression): `spawn_blocking`.

## Mutation Safety

Functions that touch filesystem, object store, or catalog MUST accept
`dry_run: bool`. When `true`: log intent via `tracing::info!`, execute nothing.

```rust
// ✅
async fn ingest_files(files: &[FileInfo], dry_run: bool) -> Result<()> {
    if dry_run {
        tracing::info!(count = files.len(), "dry run: would ingest files");
        return Ok(());
    }
    // actual I/O here
    Ok(())
}
```

## Dependencies

- Check `Cargo.toml` before adding any `use` statement for external crates.
- Prefer `std` over new crate. Prefer existing crate over adding another.
- Adding a heavy crate (async runtime, framework, serialization): ask first.

## Testing

- Unit test pure logic in `domain/`, `config/`, `lakehouse/schema.rs`.
- Integration test I/O boundaries with `testcontainers-rs`.
- Use `tempfile` for filesystem tests. No hardcoded paths.
- `#[tokio::test]` for async tests. `#[test]` for sync.
